{title: Fairest Lord Jesus}
{lyricist: Münster Gesangbuch}
{translator: Joseph A. Seiss}
{composer: Silesian folk melody}
{year: 1677}
{meta: translation-year 1873}
{meta: tune-year 1842}
{key: D}
{meta: tune ST. ELIZABETH (CRUSADERS' HYMN)}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to ST. ELIZABETH}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags praise, creation}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Fairest Lord [G]Jesus,
[D]Ruler of [A]all na[D]ture,
O [G]Thou of [D]God and [Em]man the [A]Son,
[D]Thee will I [G]cherish,
[D]Thee will I [A]honor,
[D]Thou, my soul's [G]glory, [D]joy, [A]and [D]crown.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Fair are the [G]meadows,
[D]Fairer still the [A]wood[D]lands,
[G]Robed in the [D]blooming [Em]garb of [A]spring;
[D]Jesus is [G]fairer,
[D]Jesus is [A]purer,
[D]Who makes the [G]woeful [D]heart [A]to [D]sing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Fair is the [G]sunshine,
[D]Fairer still the [A]moon[D]light,
And [G]all the [D]twinkling [Em]starry [A]host;
[D]Jesus shines [G]brighter,
[D]Jesus shines [A]purer
[D]Than all the [G]angels [D]heaven [A]can [D]boast.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Beautiful [G]Savior!
[D]Lord of all [A]the na[D]tions!
[G]Son of [D]God and [Em]Son of [A]Man!
[D]Glory and [G]honor,
[D]Praise, ado[A]ration,
[D]Now and for[G]ever[D]more [A]be [D]Thine.
{end_of_verse}
